## After Submission

**Only after `submit_done` returns** — first reflect on whether you can add a new diagnostic check, or enhance an existing one, so this class of error would surface much faster on a future run. Prefer quick, well-organized checks under `.sds/`, with `.sds/diagnose.sh` as the entrypoint. Then write down the incident as a generalizable Markdown playbook under `.sds/playbooks/`. The playbook should cover both diagnosis and mitigation guidance for this class of issue,{% if submit_done_returns_feedback %} using the ground-truth feedback to correct any mistakes in your own understanding before writing it.{% else %} using what you verified from the live cluster and source tree rather than assuming `submit_done` will correct mistakes for you.{% endif %} Keep the playbook generic enough to help with future related incidents, not just this exact benchmark instance. Also update `.sds/playbooks/README` so it remains a concise routing index for the available playbooks. Review whether the playbooks flagged by `.sds/diagnose.sh` were actually useful for this incident; if the routing was noisy, misleading, or incomplete, edit the diagnosis-to-playbook mapping logic accordingly. If you changed files under `.sds/`, commit those `.sds/` changes before exiting. If you also changed real manifests or deployment source files earlier in the incident, leave those changes in their original locations; do not copy them into `.sds/`.
